Z||000000||MooCow||12-25-2000||09:56 PM||||I was wondering if any of you know how short the shorten shifters are?  I am asking because I may buy one and he said that it is from an 84 but is about 1 inch shorter than the 85-88 ones?  Is that the shorten shifter or are they smaller?  Also how much would it cost if I bought this one to become as short as the rest if needed?  Cause I can get this one for $15.<P>                            Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||GeeDee86GT||12-25-2000||10:44 PM||||Ken:  Randy Agee provides some excellent instructions on how to shorten your shifter. The 84 shifter is the bottom one in the first picture, and is the shortest stock shifter.  If you cut and weld your own it can be even shorter. It's at: <A HREF="http://fierozone.tripod.com/weekend/shifter/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fierozone.tripod.com/weekend/shifter/index.html</A> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/garby_d/siggy.jpg"> ||||reg||12
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||12-25-2000||10:53 PM||||MooCow, This should give you the info you need:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/shifter.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com/shifter.htm</A> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723593&p=35728572&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P><BR>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 12-25-2000).]||||reg||1
