Z||000006||DXR_DAD||12-26-2000||04:01 PM||||MooCow, that shift knob is a Grant carbon fiber/leather it came from a local speed shop<P>It matches the wheel  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723593&p=35728575&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P><BR>DXR_DAD<P>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 12-26-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 12-26-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000007||Cheever2||12-26-2000||07:13 PM||||How do you get the boot off?  I don't want to tear up anything trying to find out without asking first.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000008||2xsess||12-26-2000||07:44 PM||||Cheever, To get the boot off you have to unscrew the knob and remove the shifter plate, once you take that off you flip it over and the are 4 nuts on the bottom. Those hold the boot on.<P>Ken, I have one of FieroDaves short shifters, it's awesome. The first day or two it was wierd trying to get used to it but now I'll have one in any stick Fiero I ever own. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I'll take some pics tomorrow and post them. I'll email you a few of my white gauges too. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||DXR_DAD||12-26-2000||08:02 PM||||Shifter plate is held on by 4 screws, under the ash trays. Also get Rodneys metal boot ring to replace the factory plastic ring!!!<BR>and if you get a realy short shifter I think it's better to replace to boot also (just for the looks) My boot is a Mr. Mikes leather<BR>short shifter boot. The shifter rod comes up through the center of the boot not that funny stock offset. You'll see what I mean when you get it in.||||reg||1
Z||000010||2xsess||12-27-2000||01:26 AM||||DXR_DAD, do you know if MrMike is still selling those boots? May I ask how much it cost you?<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||DXR_DAD||12-27-2000||10:59 AM||||Jeff, I don't remember the $$ but I'm sure Mr. Mike still has or will make the boots<BR>I also got the ebrake boot to match.<BR>And what ever the price was it was not that much for nice soft leather boots!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I can look in my file and see if I can get you the price later tonight????||||reg||1
